WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.130
You don't wanna miss
important notifications,

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.140
but you also don't wanna be overloaded

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.690
with updates about things
you might not care about.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.670
So let's talk about how
you can customize your

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.500
notifications in Basecamp.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.330
First, where do you
find your notifications?

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.100
The answer is your sidebar.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.260
So you can find that at
the bottom right corner,

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.420
just clicking that area open.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.590
You can also type SHIFT+S
from your keyboard to pop

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.350
that open SHIFT+S again, to close it.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.720
When you're in your sidebar,
you can click into any

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.480
of these notifications in
that "New for you" section,

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.230
and it will take you directly
to that item in Basecamp.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.970
One of the great things about Basecamp is

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.050
how flexible it is,

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.900
and you get to decide what
you're notified about versus

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.030
what stays a little more quiet.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.610
So let's jump into a project.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.180
At the top right corner,
you'll see this area

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.360
where we'll indicate what your
notification settings are.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.520
So if I have notifications on,

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.980
I'm gonna be looped in when new things are

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.570
posted to this project.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.280
Now, if this is a project
you don't need to be

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.930
as involved in, you can choose

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.900
to only be notified when
someone at mentions you

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.540
or replies to a thread
that you're following.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.850
So you get to decide
from project to project

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.640
how involved your notifications are.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.710
There are some additional
notification settings

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.990
that you can get to by clicking
your avatar in the bottom

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:18.570
left corner, going to
accounts and settings,

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.940
and then notification settings.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.230
There's also an easier way to get there.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.640
If you hit SHIFT+J

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.490
and pop open that jump
menu, you can type in

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.290
that search bar notifications

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:31.620
and your notification settings
will pop up. On this page,

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.470
you have lots of options
for Basecamp notifications,

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.540
including what we notify you about,

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.490
how we notify you and when.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.200
Just a couple things to point out.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.530
We automatically will send you
a notification when you have

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.110
an upcoming event or
something on the schedule.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.340
Those come out the day

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.260
before the event as
well as an hour before.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.510
But if those aren't
reminders that you need,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.370
you can simply uncheck that.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.960
Same thing with upcoming assignments.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.270
You can choose if we send
you reminders in your

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.730
notifications about things
that are coming due.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.070
You also have options
with email notifications.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.620
I'm personally in Basecamp
all day every day,

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.930
so I don't also need a separate email,

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.510
but that's something you might
choose to turn on or off.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.790
So just take a look through these options

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.110
and make some decisions.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:14.220
Two things I wanna point out

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.980
for ways you can turn off
notifications completely.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.830
And the first is called Work Can Wait.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.170
You can choose what
times of the day, as well

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.310
as what days of the week

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.600
you get notifications.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.260
So if you don't want
notifications before 8:00 AM

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.840
or you don't want
notifications on the weekends,

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.210
you can change those
settings here as well.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.450
Another way to turn off
notifications is if you're maybe in

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.420
a meeting or you wanna
just do some focused work,

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.330
you can temporarily silence
those notifications.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:45.450
So from your sidebar,
again, that's SHIFT+S,

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.000
you can hit this Shhhhh! button

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.900
and your notifications will
temporarily be silenced.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.120
With that sidebar closed, you don't see

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.790
that you have any notifications at all.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.320
And when you're ready to
come off of that silent mode,

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.240
just head back to that sidebar.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.280
You can click to release those,

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.160
and any notifications you
have will pop right back up.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.720
And while we're talking
about notifications,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.070
I wanna point out one other way

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:11.920
you can get alerts about what's
happening in your account.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.770
From the activity screen
right here at the top,

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:16.840
at the top right, you'll see an option

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.930
to have an email summary of everything

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:21.250
that's happened in your account.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:22.300
So check that

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.540
and you'll be getting an
email summary every morning at

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.780
7:00 AM your local
time, giving you a rundown

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.480
of everything that's happened
within your account that day.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.850
I personally like getting
that email every day just

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:35.770
to give me a rundown of what's happened

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:36.880
and make sure there's nothing

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.740
that's slipped through the cracks.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:41.380
How you wanna be notified in
Basecamp is very personal,

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.690
so play around with it,
see what works for you.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.860
You can always make changes

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:46.720
as you're getting more used to Basecamp.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.940
If you have questions about
anything I've covered in this

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:50.470
Basecamp Basic series, reach out

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:53.380
to our support team at
support@basecamp.com.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.750
Someone's around 24/7 to help you out.

